-- title:
--   Germ of q regular and stalk dimension ≥ 2 at a crossing
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N_0 \neq 0$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`, i.e. the bundled data of a proper flat integral model $X(N_0,q)$ over $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{R}\,q)$ together with its normality, its generic smoothness and geometric integrality, a curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ identified with the base change of the model, Galois equivariance and Igusa-chart pinning data, and the sections $\varepsilon_\infty, \varepsilon_0$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain, $\rho_O : \mathrm{R}\,q \to O$ a ring homomorphism, and assume the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by the image of $q$; let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ a ring homomorphism. Write $X_O = \mathtt{DRLevel.XO}\ \rho_O$ for the base change of the model along $\rho_O$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two morphisms $\mathfrak{X}.\mathtt{comp}\ \kappa\ (\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O)\ 0$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\mathtt{comp}\ \kappa\ (\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O)\ 1$ (the two components of the fibre over $\kappa$), and let $x_n = \mathfrak{X}.\mathtt{crossingPt}\ \rho_O\ \mathrm{to}\kappa\ n$ be its image in $X_O$ under the first projection followed by the $0$-component map followed by the base-change map. Assume that both $\mathfrak{X}.\xi_\infty$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\xi_0$ specialise to $x_n$. Then the germ at $x_n$ of the global section of $X_O$ obtained by pulling back $q \in O$ along the structure morphism $X_O \to \operatorname{Spec} O$ is a non-zero-divisor in the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X_O, x_n}$, and $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} \mathcal{O}_{X_O, x_n} \ge 2$ in $\mathbb{N}_\infty \cup \{\bot\}$.
--
--   This records the two local facts about the Deligne–Rapoport model of the modular curve of level $N_0 q$ at a point where the two components of the characteristic-$q$ fibre cross: the uniformiser of the base is a regular element of the local ring, and that local ring has dimension at least two. It feeds the construction of oriented crossing charts at such points, [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart).
